Viktor 10.10.2026: «И по Trash хотел спросить... картинки у нас куда удаляются с обложек треков и остального? Может отдельный Trash сделать в колонке воркспейсов? `Trash (Art)`. Вижу Trash у Артиста, но пока что очистки и удаления нет.»

The art put away lies in three places: the Artist's runs in the trash (trash/artist/), the pictures put aside (in their runs still), the covers taken off the takes (each take's artwork-removed/: by a redraw, by Remove, by a new cover). The library's column, under Out of sight, has Trash (Art): the three in one list with a picture beside each line, their number in the column, what they weigh; ticked, given back (a cover given back to its take, the one it has now kept in its place) or deleted for good, asked first with what goes and how much; none ticked, Wipe out the art's trash. A frozen workspace's covers stay as they are and say why. There Ctrl+A ticks no take and Delete sends none to the trash; Empty by itself stays the takes' trash's own. The Artist's Trash look: Delete for good on each run and on each picture put aside, Wipe out for all it shows (never the covers: the library's Trash (Art) has them), each asked first. The lab's side: GET /artist/bin, GET /artist/bin-file, POST /artist/bin {op: restore | delete | empty, items}.

Suite: 619/0 in the kitchen.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
